# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings so they run on macOS/Linux even when
# the repo is checked out on Windows (this repo is developed on Windows). A
# CRLF in the shebang or a command line breaks the script on a Mac.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Dependency source patches (applied by `cargo patch-crate`) must keep LF: the
# crates they patch ship with LF sources, and a CRLF checkout would make every
# hunk fail to match.
patches/*.patch text eol=lf
